# Every endpoint except /health needs an Entra ID access token for THIS API
# (role: Recruiter or HiringManager). With the Azure CLI signed in as a user who has a role:
#   az account get-access-token --scope <scope> --query accessToken -o tsv
# where <scope> is api_scopes.job from: terraform -chdir=infra/identity output api_scopes
# Tokens last about an hour.
@token = paste-token-here
@host = http://localhost:5102

### Create a job
POST {{host}}/jobs
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Senior .NET Engineer",
  "description": "Build microservices on Azure.",
  "location": "Remote"
}

### List all jobs
GET {{host}}/jobs
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get a job by id (replace the id)
GET {{host}}/jobs/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update a job (replace the id)
PUT {{host}}/jobs/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Staff .NET Engineer",
  "description": "Build microservices on Azure.",
  "location": "Hybrid"
}

### Health check
GET {{host}}/health
